/-!
# KFB: Gaussian-integer data on item stacks, linear-combination expressions

* `GI = ℤ × ℤ` (Gaussian integer `a + b i`), stored on a stack as the two items `a, b`
  (`gflat`).  `toC` is the embedding into `ℂ`; `gmul` the product.
* `lcE l`: the register expression `Σ c_t · top(r_t)` for coefficients `c_t ∈ {-1, 0, 1}`, built
  only from `add`, `neg`, `reg`, `lit` (a linear expression: cost `O(size · (B + 2))`).
  `lcE_eval`, `lcE_bnd` (all partial sums of `n ≤ 2^e` terms of size `≤ w` have size `≤ w + e`).
* `FSp.mvN`: the fine counted move with the count read from a register and its loop overhead
  bounded by the count itself (`≤ N (250 w + 1600) + 2000`, no `Bb`).
-/

